.TH "pocket_snap" "1" "" "" "Pocket SDR"
.SH NAME
pocket_snap \- Snapshot positioning from IF data
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
pocket_snap [\-ts time] [\-pos lat,lon,hgt] [\-ti sec] [\-toff toff]
            [\-f freq] [\-fi freq] [\-tint tint] [\-sys sys[,...]]
            [\-verb] [\-w file] [\-v] \-nav file [\-out file] file
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Snapshot positioning from a digitized IF data file.
The command searches GNSS signals over a short integration window, resolves ms ambiguities in code offsets using a coarse position (or a Doppler\-only solution if no coarse position is given), and
estimates the receiver position by least\-squares from the resolved code offsets.
.SH OPTIONS ([]: DEFAULT)
.TP
\f[CR]\-ts time\f[R]
Capture start time in UTC, as \f[CR]YYYY/MM/DD HH:MM:SS\f[R].
[parsed from the file name]
.TP
\f[CR]\-pos lat,lon,hgt\f[R]
Coarse receiver position (latitude/longitude in deg, height in m).
[no coarse position]
.TP
\f[CR]\-ti sec\f[R]
Time interval between snapshots in s.
\f[CR]0.0\f[R] = single snapshot.
[\f[CR]0.0\f[R]]
.TP
\f[CR]\-toff toff\f[R]
Time offset from the start of the IF data in s.
[\f[CR]0.0\f[R]]
.TP
\f[CR]\-f freq\f[R]
Sampling frequency of the IF data in MHz.
[\f[CR]12.0\f[R]]
.TP
\f[CR]\-fi freq\f[R]
IF frequency in MHz.
\f[CR]0\f[R] = IQ (zero\-IF).
[\f[CR]0.0\f[R]]
.TP
\f[CR]\-tint tint\f[R]
